Apple today released new firmware for its second-generation <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airtag/">AirTag</a> item trackers. The firmware has a 3.0.49 version number, up from 3.0.45, and it is the second firmware update that Apple has provided for the &zwnj;AirTag&zwnj; 2.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1033746" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/01/Second-Generation-AirTag-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="1018" height="572" /><br/>
There is no word yet on what's included in the firmware, but &zwnj;AirTag&zwnj; firmware updates most often address bugs and make other under-the-hood improvements. Apple's prior firmware update tweaked the unwanted tracking sound to make it easier to find an unknown &zwnj;AirTag&zwnj; when using Precision Finding.<br/>
<br/>
Apple will provide details on what's in the 3.0.49 firmware when it updates its <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102183">firmware support page</a>.<br/>
<br/>
For the original &zwnj;AirTag&zwnj;, firmware was distributed on a rolling basis over two weeks, but Apple appears to be pushing firmware updates to all &zwnj;AirTag&zwnj; 2 users at the same time.<br/>
<br/>
You can <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/how-to/check-airtags-firmware-version/">check your AirTag firmware</a> by opening the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/find-my/">Find My</a> app, going to the Items tab, selecting an &zwnj;AirTag&zwnj; in the list, and tapping on the &zwnj;AirTag&zwnj;'s name to see its firmware version.<br/>
<br/>
